stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR
    [*] --> ON: K1 provisioned with no sector profile
    [*] --> OFF: K2 provisioned RBI, SEBI or IRDAI, or AI declined at onboarding
    OFF --> ENABLE_PENDING: K3 tenant admin requests enablement
    ENABLE_PENDING --> ON: K4 distinct checker approves and an eligible provider exists
    ENABLE_PENDING --> OFF: K5 checker rejects or request withdrawn
    ON --> OFF: K6 any tenant admin switches off, no checker
    ON --> SUSPENDED: K7 incident owner contains an AI or provider fault
    ENABLE_PENDING --> SUSPENDED: K7 incident owner contains an AI or provider fault
    SUSPENDED --> ON: K8 incident owner lifts containment
    SUSPENDED --> OFF: K9 tenant admin switches off during suspension
    ON --> ON: K10 per-feature opt-out or checked opt-in
    ON --> OFF: K11 sector profile changes to RBI, SEBI or IRDAI

    note right of ON
      Narrowing is single-actor and immediate.
      Widening is maker-checked.
      The chokepoint re-reads the state on
      every call - it is the enforcement point.
    end note

    note right of SUSPENDED
      Only the incident owner lifts it.
      A tenant may still switch off.
    end note
